# Stages of Journey:
 # Different parts of the application: 
 1) Three Live BuildUnits - 
    status of choosen three buildunits in terms of the following:
    proportion of work completed; proportion of days worked compared to 
    alloted number of days; proportion of budget money used

 2) All BuildUnits -
    collage of different buildUnits - planned, current, completed

 3) Profile - 
    Personal details

 4) Messages - 
    all direct messages across different domain channels with a link to the conversation; 
    direct messages not linked to any channel;

 5) Organization - 
    start project, buildunit, channels, teams, members etc
 
 6) Three Live Channels -
    status of choosen domain channels in terms of the following:
    any outstanding item from me; latest message in the channel;
    current outstanding item of the channel; time spent in this channel;

 7) All domain Channels -
    collage of domain channels - across all domains

 7) BuildUnit -
    all domain channels; current outstanding item details;
    all the metrics from live buildunit widget

 8) Channel - 
    chat history, list of participants in the channel with an option to send direct message,
    all the metrics from live channel widget

 9) Three Live Projects:
    status of choosen three projects in terms of the following:
    proportion of work completed in buildunits, days worked;

10) All Projects: 
    Collage of different projects - across regions

11) Project: 
    collage of all BuildUnits, all the metrics from live project widget

12) Landing Page:
    has a navigation bar with logo, About Us, Resources, Pricing, Login and Signup;
    has hero section divided into two parts - a short video to illustrate how application works 
    and a carousel to diplay important features of the application;
    has a footer section with logo, Product Features, Resources, Connect

13) Signup: 
    two options - (email and password) or (social media - gmail) 

14) login:
    either with (email and password) or with (otp to email or mobile) or with social media (gmail) 

# Client journey on a typical day:
  Three Live BuildUnits ---> BuildUnit
                                  --> current outstanding item
				  --> different domain channel ---> Channel

# Architect journey on a typical day:
  Three Live Projects ---> Project
                               --> different BuildUnits ---> BuildUnit
			                                          --> current outstanding item
								  --> different domain channels ---> Channel
# Supervisor journey on a typical day:
  Three Live Channels ---> Channel ---> Chat
  
# HeadMason journey on a typical day:
  Channel ---> Chat

# Login with otp to email:
  landing Page ---> login
                      --> with email and password
                      --> with otp
                            --> to email ---> initialLoginPage
			    --> to mobile 
                      --> with social media (gmail)

                       
  
				  
    

